 "name": "Marshall Bluesbreaker (Aion Cerulean)",
 "version": {
  "major": 1,
  "minor": 0
 },
 "description": "Marshall Bluesbreaker (1991) as Aion FX's Cerulean (document 2.0.1), with true bypass: two op-amp stages sharing the Drive pot, the first's feedback in its top half and the second's input through its bottom half, then soft clipping in the second stage's feedback, Tone and Volume. Aion's additions, from the Analogman King of Tone: a Clipping switch (soft, the stock Bluesbreaker's; none, a boost; or hard, to VB), a Mode switch between the pre-1995 and post-1995 values, and an internal Gain DIP shifting Drive's range up.",
 "tags": [
  "overdrive"
 ],
